# Supabase Configuration for Oquvi
# IMPORTANT:
# 1. Create a file named .env in the project root by copying this file:
#    cp .env.example .env
# 2. Replace the placeholder values below with your real Supabase credentials.
# 3. Where to find these in Supabase:
#    - Sign in to https://supabase.com/dashboard
#    - Select your project (or create a free new one)
#    - Navigate to: Project Settings -> API
#    - Copy "Project URL" into VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#    - Copy "Project API Keys" -> "anon public" into VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# 4. NEVER put your service_role secret key in this frontend file.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key-here
